  "question": {
    "text": "Two dice are tossed once. The probability of getting an even number at the first die or a total of 8 is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rQj6X",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{36}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Jwsph",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{36}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fUxKR",
      "text": "$\\frac{11}{36}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VyFSY",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: $A=$ getting even no on 1st dice\n$$\n\\mathrm{B}=\\text { getting sum } 8\n$$\nSo $|\\mathrm{A}|=18 \\quad|\\mathrm{~B}|=5 \\quad|\\mathrm{~A} \\cap \\mathrm{B}|=3$\n\n$$\n\\text { So } P(A \\cup B)=\\frac{18+5-3}{36}=\\frac{20}{36} \\text {}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
